WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.734
And I want to go now to

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:02.402
Bill Browder, longtime Putin critic.

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.670
He's wanted in Russia

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:06.072
and the retired Army Lieutenant General

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:06.873
Ben Hodges.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:07.507
And I appreciate

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.242
both of you very much, Bill.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:09.943
So obviously,

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:10.944
we haven't seen Prigozhin

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:13.079
since that armed rebellion 12 days ago.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.848
The part of the deal that was announced

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.416
was he was going to Belarus,

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:17.283
but Lukashenko says

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.218
he's in Saint Petersburg,

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:20.120
maybe in Moscow,

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.921
and we're seeing but he's a free man.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.156
He can you can do whatever he wants.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.025
And I talk to him on the phone yesterday,

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.593
even though they've raided his houses

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:27.761
and taken everything out of it

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:28.895
in a humiliating end

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:30.196
with all these wigs and everything else

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.297
that they're parading around.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:32.699
What is going on here, Bill?

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.769
Well, I think first and foremost, I mean,

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:36.503
he is he's

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:37.771
committed the cardinal

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:40.240
sin of making Putin look weak.

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:42.208
Putin prides himself

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.411
on being a strongman dictator.

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:47.947
And Prigozhin basically put a whole slice

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.582
that that reputation

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:52.352
in half by marching on Rostov.

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.553
Nobody stood in his way.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.788
They were cheering him

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.923
on, taking selfies with him,

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.525
going on to Virgin Edge.

00:00:58.525 --> 00:00:59.125
And then

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.327
getting within 2 hours of Moscow.

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.496
He's kind of a folk hero in Russia,

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:04.597
and he makes Putin

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.266
look like a very weak man.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.200
And so

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:08.968
what's going on right now is

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.805
the Russians are in a state of apoplexy.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.740
Putin particularly because

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.141
he's been challenged,

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.476
his entire

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:17.444
sort of strongman

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:19.712
image has been challenged So Prigozhin

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.882
surely doesn't want to be found

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:23.450
right now.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.451
I can imagine that

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:25.852
if they're doing all these movies

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:26.252
and opening

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.088
these criminal cases against him,

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.222
they would love to kill him

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.390
if they could get their hands on him.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:33.026
And so he's probably gone to ground.

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.194
He's a very dangerous man.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:36.162
He has a whole army of mercenaries

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.597
and people loyal to him. Yes.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.999
And and what we're seeing right now is

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.501
you think he's gone to ground and

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:42.936
he's alive in Russia.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:44.904
Who knows?

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.873
I mean, he has so many different ways.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.875
We saw the wigs we saw the passports.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.176
We saw the cache.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.278
There was a helicopter,

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:53.913
you know, in his front yard.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.115
He's got all I mean,

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.649
this man is incredible

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.751
in terms of the tools that he has

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:02.388
to, you know, evade capture.

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:03.690
I mean, he he's

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.591
he's the most cold

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.725
blooded killer out there.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.861
And so he's not going to allow himself

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.062
to be handcuffed

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:12.799
and carted away to Lubyanka, the prison.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.834
Well, it's not that's not happened.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:15.468
And so,

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:16.069
you know,

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:17.403
everyone says you know,

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.139
how much longer does he have to live?

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:19.706
Well, you know,

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:20.940
he's got all these killers

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.941
on his payroll.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.243
How much longer do these guys,

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:25.445
the FSB, Putin himself,

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.480
have to live with this type of scenario

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.348
playing itself out?

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:29.215
I mean, General Hodges,

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.116
it is incredible

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:31.117
and it is incredible

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.452
what they're showing us, right.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:34.154
That he's nowhere to be found.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:36.689
And as

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:37.090
they're rating

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.858
his houses and showing those wigs

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:39.993
and those things,

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.461
what does this say to you

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.429
from a military perspective?

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.231
Putin says the deal is,

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.499
well, we're told right.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.735
The deal is promotion goes to Belarus.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:49.369
Belarus says,

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:49.969
oh, he's not here,

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:50.703
he's in Moscow

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:51.671
or Saint Petersburg,

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:54.374
and he's completely M.I.A.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.543
So three things there.

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:59.612
First of all, how can anybody

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:02.348
seriously consider negotiations

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.383
with Russia

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:04.083
and expect

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.985
that they would live up to any agreement

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.253
or that they'll be transparent

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:07.887
in any way?

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:08.655
I mean, the

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:09.355
the circus

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.023
that we've been watching

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.824
in the last couple of weeks, tragic

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:13.426
and that people are getting killed.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:15.461
But there are a lot of people

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.330
that think that we should push Ukraine

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.731
to negotiate with Russia.

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:21.301
This is who you're negotiating with.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:22.335
Secondly,

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:23.536
the kind of activities

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:24.671
that we have seen here

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:25.905
over the last several days,

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:29.042
including when President Putin wilted,

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:30.777
when he was pushed into a corner,

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:32.946
he wilted and turned to Lukashenko

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:36.082
and they made this deal with Prigozhin,

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.017
which obviously is not turning out

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.285
like everybody thought

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.954
or like I thought anyhow.

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.155
But that's what he did

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:43.256
when he was put in a corner.

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.123
So it did show

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:45.692
weakness exactly as Bill said.

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:47.393
But also, finally,

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.963
this is not what happens in an army

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:50.930
that's confident

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.465
that it's on the path to victory.

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.067
So this is this really reflects

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.035
uncertainty and lack of confidence

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.804
in the government and in the Army.

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:58.171
So, Bill,

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.072
I want to play some more from

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.406
that Lukashenko press conference

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:02.342
where he took all those questions

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:04.244
from journalists and our Matthew Chance.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:07.380
He said he spoke to Prigozhin yesterday

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.048
and then unprompted,

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:10.950
he said this about promotions, safety.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:11.951
Let me play that

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.622
Listen, if you don't know

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:17.457
what will happen to Prigozhin next.

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.292
Well, everything happens in life.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.226
But if you think that Putin

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:21.261
is so malicious

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:21.961
and vindictive

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.297
that he will kill Prigozhin tomorrow.

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:27.100
No, this will not happen at

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:28.968
all. Right?

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.136
It brings it up out of the blue.

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:31.137
So that's significant.

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:31.604
Then he makes

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.573
his claim of that will not happen.

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:34.274
I mean,

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:37.443
what do you read into that statement

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:39.212
from Lukashenko?

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:40.413
Well, first of all,

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.114
all of these guys,

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:42.782
Lukashenko, Putin, Prigozhin,

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.317
you can't believe a word that they say.

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:45.718
I mean, they lied through their teeth.

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:46.986
They lie openly.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.821
So you really can't interpret

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:49.622
anything from that.

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:52.091
I mean, what I would say is that that

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:52.959
you know,

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:53.459
this guy,

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:54.460
Prigozhin,

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.395
organized an armed

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:57.263
rebellion to take out Putin.

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:58.298
The normal reaction to

00:04:58.298 --> 00:04:59.699
that would be for Putin

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.000
to arrest Prigozhin,

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.135
bring him to Red Square

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.136
and set up a guillotine

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.504
and chop his head off.

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:05.571
The fact that he didn't do

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.340
that is remarkable.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.142
The fact that they let him go somewhere,

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:11.144
whether it's Belarus or somewhere else.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.512
We just yesterday

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:13.513
they went after

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.515
they after when he was doing his raid,

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:16.883
they or his

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.985
his rebellion, they raided his office

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:21.654
and they seized $111 million of cash

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:23.890
And then as I understand it, yesterday

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.291
they returned the cash.

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.759
It makes no sense.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:29.329
And so what they're saying, there's

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:30.863
so much more to the story

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:32.432
that we don't see on the surface.

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:33.900
And you alluded to it

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.002
earlier in the report that he's got

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.570
17 different countries

00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:39.439
rebellions in

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:40.473
Africa, where

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:41.941
he's got mercenary operations

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.242
which is essentially the

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:45.645
the entire foreign policy of Russia

00:05:45.645 --> 00:05:47.847
and Africa that's under his command.

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:49.782
And so he may be just too big to

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:50.283
make out.

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:51.017
I don't know.

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:52.552
But but it's it's

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:54.420
doesn't make any sense on the surface.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.121
And therefore, there's

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:56.322
a lot of information

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.758
that we don't know, obviously

00:05:58.758 --> 00:06:00.293
guiding their their actions.

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:00.960
General Hodges,

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.228
I want to ask you one thing

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:03.363
crucial to the battlefield

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.664
in addition to all of this. Right.

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:05.732
Which could dramatically change

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:06.499
all of it.

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:08.301
And that is these cluster munitions.

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:09.035
CNN's reporting

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:11.003
the US is expected to announce

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.572
a new military package to Ukraine,

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:13.706
which is going to finally include

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.241
those cluster munitions. Right.

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:16.576
Highly controversial.

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:17.810
Banned by 100 countries,

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.345
not by the United States or Russia.

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:20.313
Incidentally,

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:20.980
they scatter

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.548
small explosives around the target.

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:24.450
So in a civilian area, it can cause

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.052
unbelievable devastation.

00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:27.253
Ukraine says they need it to hit

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:29.288
clumps of Russian soldiers

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:31.958
and that they've been saying this,

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:33.826
you know, since the very beginning.

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:36.362
How significant is this if Ukraine gets

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:37.730
these cluster munitions, that

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:40.566
this will

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:43.202
be a significant capability for Ukraine?

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:45.338
When you talk about

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:47.673
employing them against Russian trenches,

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:50.042
particularly the Russian trenches,

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:51.043
which as we've

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:51.511
all seen,

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:52.678
do not have

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.747
the overhead cover that you would expect

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:56.516
from professional soldiers.

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:57.650
So this kind of munition

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.253
will be devastating against the Russians.

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.788
Who are sitting in these trenches,

00:07:01.788 --> 00:07:03.423
which will help, obviously,

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.024
with the breakthrough

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:06.926
that Ukraine is trying to achieve.

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:08.428
And they're also devastating

00:07:08.428 --> 00:07:09.896
against artillery

00:07:09.896 --> 00:07:10.897
when the Ukrainians

00:07:10.897 --> 00:07:12.532
catch Russian artillery

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:14.300
in a woodland somewhere,

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.203
this munition will really cause problems

00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:17.904
for them.

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:19.472
And fortunately,

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:20.406
the United States has

00:07:20.406 --> 00:07:22.141
a couple of million of these rounds.

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:23.509
And so it will help

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:25.645
make up the deficiency

00:07:25.645 --> 00:07:27.246
in artillery ammunition.

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:28.648
Unfortunately,

00:07:28.648 --> 00:07:30.249
it doesn't make up the deficiency

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:32.185
in not providing the attack.

00:07:32.185 --> 00:07:33.152
No, it doesn't.

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:33.619
But, of course,

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:35.488
President Zelensky was telling us

00:07:35.488 --> 00:07:36.789
it would be crucial,

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:38.424
crucial anything to close that

00:07:38.424 --> 00:07:39.292
artillery gap.

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:40.159
As you point out,

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:41.527
that they just don't have enough.

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:41.761
All right.

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:42.895
Thank you both so very much.

00:07:42.895 --> 00:07:43.596
I appreciate it.

